I tried looking into this. I wasn't able to figure out a solution but I have a diagnosis.

The line that throws the warning is

```C++
} else if (p_variable->assignments == 0) {
	parser->push_warning(p_variable, GDScriptWarning::UNASSIGNED_VARIABLE, p_variable->identifier->name);
}
```
from [GDScriptAnalyzer::resolve_variable](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/fe01776f05b1787b28b4a270d53037a3c25f4ca2/modules/gdscript/gdscript_analyzer.cpp#L1977)

and `assignments` is set by [GDScriptParser::parse_variable](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/fe01776f05b1787b28b4a270d53037a3c25f4ca2/modules/gdscript/gdscript_parser.cpp#L1067)
```C++
if (match(GDScriptTokenizer::Token::EQUAL)) {
	// Initializer.
	variable->initializer = parse_expression(false);
	if (variable->initializer == nullptr) {
		push_error(R"(Expected expression for variable initial value after "=".)");
	}
	variable->assignments++;
}
```

Since `var a: Array[int]` has no `=` sign, `assignments` is never incremented and therefore it throws the warning
